    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups to secure our 5x5 standing. Our primary engine today is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who leads our active starters with a 74.56 score. His matchup against Burnes (xERA 5.41) provides a massive +19% boost in SP skill, and with the added utility of batting in the heart of the order, he is our premier play. **Jackson Merrill** follows closely (71.50) against Alcantara, as his elite dynamic platoon splits against right-handed pitching give him the ceiling required to chase down our stolen base and batting average targets. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start despite facing a formidable arm in Misiorowski (xERA 2.32); while his raw SP skill score takes a hit, the +16% park adjustment keeps him in elite territory (67.74).\n\nThe decision to bench **Josh Jung** (43.41) was the most difficult call of the day. While **Josh Jung** possesses strong upside, he fell just short of our threshold due to the looming threat of the opposing starter, Miles, and the superior efficiency ratings afforded to **Sam Antonacci** and **Wade Meckler** in more advantageous situational spots. We are also closely monitoring the lineup status of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Luis Lara**; should those \"Lineup Pending\" designations shift significantly downward, we may be forced to look toward the bench to preserve our limited game caps. \n\nFinally, a note on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.39). While he remains in the UTIL slot, caution is warranted; facing deGrom is never optimal, and the -19% SP skill penalty significantly compresses his ceiling. We are gambling on his ability to drive in runs for the Austin Waves despite the elite-level opposition. We remain vigilant regarding the health of **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose continued absence forces us to squeeze every ounce of value from the remaining active roster, particularly with **Nasim Nunez** providing critical, albeit marginal, versatility in the nine-hole.",
